{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4a573e7bfd1e047000fc3b0335a4fb147a9e64145b43ec960122d6393dbfdf03","digest":{"component_or_area":"build/lint infrastructure","key_entities":["scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","Makefile","lint target","tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","scripts/gen_env_registry.py","tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["comment-hygiene gate","make lint","local vs CI divergence","gate wiring"],"propositions":["The comment-hygiene gate runs in CI as a standalone step but is not wired into the local make lint target, causing local lint to pass while CI rejects the same tree","The gate's test coverage runs only in the full test suite, not in make lint, delaying detection of hygiene violations until CI review","The introducing ticket shows no deliberate intent to exclude the gate from make lint; it follows the scripts/check_*.py convention modeled on existing gates","Adding the gate to make lint adds ~4.9s runtime overhead, acceptable relative to the 15-minute CI cycle cost of a local miss","The wiring should mirror the precedent of scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check, which is already in the lint target with a documented rationale"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787776452484812001,"uuid":"0f7ab82c-b575-4341-8856-222d250799b3"}